email.task:
You are an IT support technician. More and more teams in your company are using DriveHub, the company's file sharing service. Carlos, a new project manager, needs to share his project files with his team. Write an email to Carlos explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- imperatives and sequence words for the steps;
- at least one sentence describing a current trend (present continuous or more and more), for example about how many teams are using DriveHub;
- at least one second conditional sentence (If + past simple, … would/could + verb), for example to explain what would happen if he chose "Can edit";
- at least one polite request (Could you…? / It would be great if you could…), for example asking Carlos to send you a screenshot.
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
